guide forever/reputation/centaur-clans
title Gelkis and Magram Centaur Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · World
levels 30-60
zone Desolace
keywords Gelkis Clan Centaur, Magram Clan Centaur, centaur, Desolace, Uthek the Wise, Warug, Captain Pentigast, Gurda Wildmane, Molkar, Gorhak, Buying Friendship, Economic Warfare, Carved Centaur Totem, Maraudine, Valley of Bones, Shen'dralas, Nerlokh, Orgrul, Hagiak, Rokren, Mulara, Magram Front, Outcast Hideaway, Bristleback Retreat, Khan Jehn, Ongeku, Kolkar, Centaur Banner Deployment Device, A Conqueror's Crown, Conqueror's Helm, title
why Desolace's feuding clans, reworked in Forever: pick one, buy its friendship, and trade totems for recipes.
reward item 269901
reward text 12 recipes for Carved Centaur Totems at the clan quartermasters, no standing needed
reward text Khan Jehn's quest: a clan title and a choice of three rare level 35 weapons

# Built from Forever's data: both clans start Neutral 2,000 (Forever's client faction table; Friendly is 1,000
# away, Honored 7,000, Revered 19,000, Exalted 40,000); the kill rows (a Magram kill gives the Gelkis 20 and
# costs the Magram 100, and the other way round; players' recordings agree, Shen'dralas's Magram Necromancers
# included, and show Khan Jehn and the Magram Bonepaws paying the same, Warug's bodyguards 5 and 25, where the kill
# rows have 100 and 500); the quest rows with Forever's values (the choice quests Strange Alliance, Gelkis Alliance,
# Brutal Politics and Magram Alliance 250; Raid on the Kolkar, Assault on the Kolkar, Stealing Supplies and Broken
# Tears 500; Ongeku and Gizmo for Warug 1,000); Forever's new quests: Buying Friendship 3,000 (needs Neutral),
# Economic Warfare 750 for 5 Carved Centaur Totems (repeatable), the profession turn-ins 1,000 (Friendly), A
# Conqueror's Crown 1,000 (Friendly), the Valley of Bones quests 125 to 500 (Honored) and Khan Jehn 6,000 with a
# title and a choice of rare weapons (Forever's quest pages; the weapons' kind and stats from the client item
# table); the totem drops (Maraudine centaurs) and Gorhak's 12 recipes. The totems bind to no one (client item
# table): they trade and sell.
# Every clan quest costs the other clan five times what it pays: the server's quest records in players' caches
# give each one the other clan's loss, and players' recordings show it on the choice quests (3 and 4 people),
# Buying Friendship (3,000 and -15,000), Economic Warfare (750 and -3,750) and the Kolkar quests, 2026-11-12.
# Molkar's spot (35.6,92.0) came from a beta player's report; the data now has him at 35.7,92.2.
# The Valley of Bones is a subzone of Shen'dralas, Forever's new zone south of Desolace (client area table). Its
# quests, givers, items and order come from Forever's quest data and the server's quest records; the spots from
# the data and players' sightings (Nerlokh, Orgrul, the valley's mobs). Nobody who records has done a valley
# quest yet, so its steps say they follow the quest data. Each asks "<clan> (Honored)" as a quest-log objective
# (Forever's quest pages; Checking Things Out and Long-Term Solutions do not).
# Test Your Theory (93045) and the Magram's Valley of Bones, Mountain of Bones and Outcast Necromancers (92841,
# 92844, 92846) are open to every race in the server's records; QuestieDB narrows them to one side (corrections
# in forever-db). Khan Jehn (93196) is handed in to the risen Khan at the ritual tent: the quest data's ender.
# Elites in the valley (the data's ranks; how they react from players' recordings): Corpsefeeders (level 45,
# hostile to everyone), Magram Necrokhans (45, hostile below Neutral with the Magram, as the Magram
# Necromancers are), Outcast Necrokhans (45) in the Outcast Hideaway, Kog'thug the Brave (43) and Quolga the
# Wise (42) in Bristleback Retreat.
# INGAME: the valley chains as written: where the Accursed Skull lies, the pond east of Gelkis Village, how
# Mulara gives the Tears, the Petrified Bark trees, Warug's Imbued Tears, where Long-Term Solutions' Outcast
# Necromancers stand (players met them only between Nerlokh and Orgrul), Rokren's escort, who takes 93196.
# INGAME: Molkar's Economic Warfare (92812) is Horde-only in QuestieDB, open to every race on Forever's quest
# pages: is it offered to an Alliance Gelkis character?
# Captain Pentigast gives Buying Friendship: Magram (93226) to the Alliance as he gives the Gelkis one, and both
# factions' Buying Friendship quests wait for Carved Centaur Totems (93224 Alliance, 93225 Horde) from the same
# giver (players' recordings, 2026-11-10: Pentigast offered 93226 and 93227 to 2 people right after 93224, Gorhak
# offered 93226 to nobody; Gurda Wildmane offered 94872 and 94873 to 2 people right after 93225, and not before).
# Which clan the guide follows (#1661's sweep, 2026-11-10): the "Gelkis or Magram" step sends the character to the
# Gelkis half when they carry or handed in any Gelkis quest, else to the Magram half when they carry or handed in
# any Magram quest (Buying Friendship included), so a character with quests of both clans stays with the Gelkis.
# The step after the Gelkis half sends a Gelkis character to the recipes, past the Magram half.
# INGAME: Where do centaur kills stop: at the end of Friendly (Forever's kill rows) or at the end of Honored
# (Classic Era players report 11,999/12,000 Honored)?
# ASSUMED: The Magram's Valley of Bones needs A Conqueror's Crown first (Forever's quest pages list it in the
# Magram series between Broken Tears and Valley of Bones; the Gelkis series has no such step). Its Conqueror's
# Helm has no source in Forever's data; Warug sends you to "a crypt" in the Badlands. In-game check: does Warug
# offer Valley of Bones without it, and where is the helm?
# Low-level quests pay their full reputation in Forever at any level: in players' recordings every
# quest turn-in 10 to 29 levels above the quest paid all of it (72 turn-ins, over 40 people, 2026-11-09),
# as one beta report said (quest 456 at level 30). Classic cut it to a fifth.

step Pick your clan
  tip The Gelkis (south-west Desolace) and the Magram (south-east) are at war: every kill of one clan gives the other 20 and costs its own clan 100, and every quest of one clan costs the other five times what it pays (Buying Friendship: 3,000 for yours, 15,000 off the other), so you can only climb with one. Both start Neutral. Forever's quests are worth far more than kills now. Alliance: Captain Pentigast at Nijel's Point offers Strange Alliance (Gelkis) and Brutal Politics (Magram). Horde: Gurda Wildmane offers Gelkis Alliance and Magram Alliance. Take the one of your clan, and Carved Centaur Totems: each clan's Buying Friendship (3,000) is offered once you bring the totems back. Then tick the task. The guide goes on with the Gelkis; take the Magram's quests instead and it goes to the Magram half. Forever pays these quests in full at any level.
  accept 1382 optional only Alliance  -- Strange Alliance: Gelkis
  accept 1368 optional only Horde     -- Gelkis Alliance
  accept 93224 only Alliance          -- Carved Centaur Totems
  accept 93225 only Horde             -- Carved Centaur Totems
  task "Take the quests of one clan"

step Carved Centaur Totems
  tip The Kolkar centaurs (level 30-33) in the camps along the eastern road, south of Nijel's Point, drop the totems, and so do the Magram and the Maraudine. Bring five back, then take your clan's Buying Friendship (Gelkis below; the Magram's instead for the Magram).
  collect 254432 x5 quest 93224.1 @69.5,44.0 only Alliance -- Carved Centaur Totem: Kolkar centaurs
  collect 254432 x5 quest 93225.1 @69.5,44.0 only Horde -- Carved Centaur Totem: Kolkar centaurs
  turnin 93224 only Alliance          -- Captain Pentigast
  turnin 93225 only Horde             -- Gurda Wildmane
  accept 93227 optional only Alliance -- Buying Friendship: Gelkis
  accept 94873 optional only Horde    -- Buying Friendship: Gelkis

step Gelkis or Magram
  skipto gelkis when onquest 1382,93227,1368,94873
  skipto gelkis when turnedin 1382
